# What this test reaches for (format `<path> <name>`). Deepening mounts these
# side by side under DEEP-DEPS, so `flake.nix` sits beside `prod/`, `rust/`,
# `std/` and `stack/` exactly as they do in the repo — which is what lets the
# worker take that directory as a FLAKE ROOT and evaluate it.
#
# dev/test-stack, not std/bash: this test needs nix AND the host's store. The
# store arrives as a volume grant (CAOS_GRANT_VOLUMES=/mounted-nix), and a
# grant is read from the image's own config, so only an image that declares it
# can have it. std/caos-build depends on test-stack for the same reason.
../../dev/test-stack test-stack
../../flake.nix flake.nix
../../flake.lock flake.lock
../../prod prod
../../rust rust
../../std std
../../stack stack
